Subject: [PATCH] MFA: strip Metal address spaces from Sol tensor type arguments

Candidate compatibility fix for SDK 27 template constraints.
Changes only get_destination_cooperative_tensor type arguments: seven call
sites, ten operand types. Does not change math, tensor precision or layout.

Based on liuliu/ccv unstable retrieved 2026-09-28, matching the source
previously reviewed at 6a611be1aab6470ae279115ae4eaf7e01bc87135.
Related report: https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/issues/4533
Corresponding pattern: mlx/backend/metal/kernels/steel/attn/nax.h

Validation here: patch application and resulting-byte comparison only.
Metal compilation and numerical/performance testing must be run on a Mac.
Confirm the original error mentions an address-space-qualified operand
and a rejected template requirement before attributing the cause to this.

